      "title": "‘Cash grab’: One Nation demands up to $630,000 from Victorian election candidates",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/one-nation-to-demand-thousands-from-victorian-election-candidates-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Many applicants left feeling ‘used, lied to, misled and gaslit’, complaint letter seen by Guardian Australia says</p><ul><li><p>Listen to the Guardian podcast <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/series/guardian-australia-podcast-series\">The Populist here</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One Nation could collect as much as $633,000 from people who have put their hand up to run in the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/19/one-nation-victorian-election-candidates-michael-piastrino-elita-dabrowski-ben-lucas-ntwnfb\">Victorian state election</a>, with potential candidates questioning whether the party is staging a “cash grab”.</p><p>Guardian Australia has spoken to multiple former councillors, mayors and deputy mayors who expressed an interest in running for the party. They claim they went through what one called a “pay-to-play” application process, after which they were rejected.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/one-nation-to-demand-thousands-from-victorian-election-candidates-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-27T00:46:02"
    },
    {
      "title": "Private colleges around Australia offering last-minute discounts for diploma allegedly ‘misused by shonks’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/australia-private-colleges-discount-deregistered-management-diploma-visa-crackdown-immigration-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Federal government to deregister graduate diploma of management in October over fears it was being used by ‘non-genuine’ students to remain in country</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Private colleges are offering discounts to rush students into a diploma the federal government is cancelling over concerns it is being “misused by shonks”.</p><p>The government announced in early September it would deregister the graduate diploma of management (learning) which it suspected was being used by “non-genuine” students to remain in Australia. The course is taught by close to 450 institutions, has over 15,000 students studying currently and more than 40,000 students registered for future enrolment following completion of a different vocational course.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/australia-private-colleges-discount-deregistered-management-diploma-visa-crackdown-immigration-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-26T20:00:45"
    },
    {
      "title": "Palestinian careers adviser who was allegedly told to stop wearing keffiyeh at Sydney school sues for racial discrimination",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/palestinian-careers-adviser-who-was-allegedly-told-to-stop-wearing-keffiyeh-at-sydney-school-sues-for-racial-discrimination-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Wasim El-Haj alleges NSW government school ordered him to stop wearing symbolic garment as it ‘may cause discord’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/27/australia-news-live-anthony-albanese-openai-medicare-hack-united-nations-richard-marles-jane-hume-liberal-coalition-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A Palestinian careers adviser who was allegedly directed to stop wearing a keffiyeh at a Sydney government school because it was a symbol that “may cause discord” has lodged a racial discrimination case in the federal court against the state of New South Wales.</p><p>Wasim El-Haj, a former careers adviser at Sydney Girls High School – an inner-city selective government school – alleges the then acting principal told him in 2024 that the keffiyeh was seen as a symbol of conflict. He alleges the state’s conduct is unlawful for breaching the Racial Discrimination Act.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/27/palestinian-careers-adviser-who-was-allegedly-told-to-stop-wearing-keffiyeh-at-sydney-school-sues-for-racial-discrimination-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-26T20:00:45"
    }
  ]
